Slightly different approach: Polymorph affects the form of a
monster or player but leaves their "mind" intact somehow. So
a PC morphed into a foo still thinks as a PC (which it has to,
since the way it thinks is determined by the person behind the
keyboard, who may not be into roleplaying). The sliming attack,
on the other hand, turns a foo into a green slime, body, mind
and all. So when a PC is slimed, it isn't actually killed,
but the game ends nevertheless, since the newly born slime
doesn't have any interest in all that fuzz about the amulet.

